Phase 18 continuation — Producer send inputs and reverse API audit
Session date: 2026-10-14 UTC
Branch: `phase/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate`
Java oracle: RocketMQ client 5.5.1, pinned source `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`; reference checkout read-only.
Plans: left unchanged.

Changes and decisions
- Matched Java caller-visible `UNIQ_KEY` preparation. Single-message Producer send methods now accept `&mut Message`; eligible accumulator sends preserve the generated or supplied ID on the caller message before runtime dispatch, while direct sends mutate only after route/address checks. Retries reuse the same ID; auto-batch inputs get unique IDs.
- Added invoked Java `sendInputMutation` cases for accumulator dispatch failure and direct service-state failure. Rust regression compares both boundaries and covers supplied-ID retention, retry reuse and batch behavior. Final `fixtures/producer/core.json` SHA-256: `079e9fcac47f97f4921a823c10b02a3b0ec882c42b85c85695663530047cd23d`.
- Reverse-scan correction: `TopicPublishInfo::from_snapshot` had no Java public constructor equivalent and only internal callers, so reduced it to `pub(crate)`. Corrected the Producer matrix's backpressure helper names and made the public validation helper mappings explicit.
- Cross-checked Phase 15–17 compatibility matrices and execution records: local acceptance is recorded as verified; their Broker-backed handoff cases remain Phase 19. No plan files were changed.

